  "body": "## Summary\n\nIn the `TrustBonding.sol` contract, users can claim their rewards for Bonding TRUST tokens. These rewards can be claimed on the next epoch based on the utilization rate of the system and the users. For the first epoch , the utilization ratio is set to the maximum for all the users \n```solidity\n  function _getPersonalUtilizationRatio(address _account, uint256 _epoch) internal view returns (uint256) {\n        if (_account == address(0)) {\n            revert TrustBonding_ZeroAddress();\n        }\n\n        // If the epoch is in the future, return 0 and exit early\n        if (_epoch > currentEpoch()) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n\n        // In epochs 0 and 1, the utilization ratio is set to the maximum value (100%)\n        if (_epoch < 2) {\n            return BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR;\n        }\n\n```\nand after that, it changes based on their personal utilization ratio.\n\nBut there is a critical flaw when calculating the rewards for the user. The vulnerability exists in the `TrustBonding` contract's reward calculation logic that allows users to bond TRUST tokens at the very end of an epoch and receive the same rewards as users who bonded for the entire epoch. This undermines the fairness of the reward distribution and can be exploited for disproportionate gains.\n\n## Description\nThe contract calculates user rewards in the `claimRewards()`. This function uses the internal `_userEligibleRewardsForEpoch()` function to calculate the rewards eligible for the user in the previous epoch. The flaw is in the where the user balance is calculated using `userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd()` which in turn uses `_balanceOf(account, _epochTimestampEnd(epoch))` which does not account for the duration a user was bonded during the epoch.\n\n```solidity\n  function userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(address account, uint256 epoch) public view returns (uint256) {\n        if (account == address(0)) {\n            revert TrustBonding_ZeroAddress();\n        }\n\n        if (epoch > currentEpoch()) {\n            revert TrustBonding_InvalidEpoch();\n        }\n\n        return _balanceOf(account, _epochTimestampEnd(epoch));\n    }\n```\n## Exploit Scenario\n\nThe exploit shown below is clearly demonstrated in the Poc given below.\n\n1. Alice bonds at the start of epoch N.\n2. Charlie waits until the last second of epoch N, then bonds the same amount.\n3. Both claim rewards for epoch N in epoch N+1.\n4. Both receive the same rewards, despite Charlie being bonded for only 1 second.\n\n\n## Impact\n- Users can game the system by bonding at the last moment(at the very last second of the epoch), receiving full rewards for minimal participation Basically stealing rewards from the other users\n\n- This can lead to unfair reward distribution and undermine the protocol's intended incentives.\n\n## Recommendation\n\n- Change the reward calculation to account for the **time-weighted average** bonded balance over the epoch, not just the balance at the end.\n- Consider tracking user balances throughout the epoch or using a checkpointing mechanism to ensure rewards are proportional to the time staked.",
  "proof_of_concept": "Paste this test inside the `TrustBonding.t.sol` contract and run `forge test --mt test_Epoch_GameRewards_by_Staking_Last_sec -vv`\n\n```solidity\n function test_Epoch_GameRewards_by_Staking_Last_sec() public {\n        _createLock(users.alice);\n        _createLock(users.charlie);\n        _advanceEpochs(1);\n        _bondOneMoreToken(users.charlie);\n        _bondOneMoreToken(users.alice);\n        resetPrank(users.alice);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.alice);\n        resetPrank(users.charlie);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.charlie);\n        // /////////////////\n        // ////////////////\n        _advanceEpochs(1);\n        _bondOneMoreToken(users.charlie);\n        _bondOneMoreToken(users.alice);\n        resetPrank(users.alice);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.alice);\n        resetPrank(users.charlie);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.charlie);\n        // ///////////////////\n        // //////////////////\n        _advanceEpochs(1);\n        _bondOneMoreToken(users.charlie);\n        _bondOneMoreToken(users.alice);\n        resetPrank(users.alice);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.alice);\n        resetPrank(users.charlie);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.charlie);\n        uint256 currentEpoch = protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch();\n        uint256 currentEpochEndTimestamp = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(currentEpoch);\n        console.log(currentEpoch);\n        console.log(currentEpochEndTimestamp);\n        /**\n         * Exploit starts\n         */\n        _advanceEpochs(1);\n        // current epoch =4\n        // Alice bonds more token at the start of this epoch\n        _bondOneMoreToken(users.alice);\n        uint256 nextEpoch = currentEpoch + 1;\n        uint256 nextEpochStart = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(currentEpoch);\n        uint256 epochLength = protocol.trustBonding.epochLength();\n        uint256 EndOfNextEpoch = (nextEpochStart + (epochLength) - 1);\n        console.log(\"EndOfNextEpoch:\", EndOfNextEpoch);\n        vm.warp(EndOfNextEpoch);\n        // charlie bonds the same amount at the last second of the epoch\n        _bondOneMoreToken(users.charlie);\n        resetPrank(users.alice);\n        // both claim their previous reward on epoch 3(not needed for this test to work)\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.alice);\n        resetPrank(users.charlie);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.charlie);\n        uint256 currentEpoch2 = protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch();\n        console.log(currentEpoch2);\n        console.log(\"alice balance at the end:\", users.alice.balance);\n        console.log(\"charlie balance at the end:\", users.charlie.balance);\n        // we wrap the timestamp to epoch 5 so that both of them can claim the reward for the 4th epoch\n        vm.warp(6_048_000 + 1);\n        uint256 currentEpoch5 = protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch();\n        console.log(currentEpoch5);\n        uint256 expectedRewardsForAlice =\n            protocol.trustBonding.userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(users.alice, protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch() - 1);\n        uint256 expectedRewardsForCharlie =\n            protocol.trustBonding.userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(users.charlie, protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch() - 1);\n        console.log(\"expectedRewardsForAlice:\", expectedRewardsForAlice);\n        console.log(\"expectedRewardsForCharlie:\", expectedRewardsForCharlie);\n        // assertion showing both alice and charlie claimed the same reward eventhough charlie bonded the tokens for only 1\n        // second in the previous epoch\n        assertEq(expectedRewardsForAlice, expectedRewardsForCharlie);\n    }\n```",
